"7042016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0b3813e3a5e52b12dc56d1b7ab7235781fb95a7fbd0effdfa2b22361cd372b0d","compact":"f5ed033556a2039fd6084257d1deddfa439e973900392f7fa8d445484c3de90e","nasal":"f5ed033556a2039fd6084257d1deddfa439e973900392f7fa8d445484c3de90e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-42-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":42,"verse":17,"english":"Rävaņa did forcibly place Sītā on her lap; how can then Rāma enjoy delight in her company? Having taken her to the city of Lankā, Rāvaņa did keep her in the Asoka forest and Sītā was brought under the control of Rākşasas. Still Rāma has not been worked up with hatred by Sītā. From now we shall also broke the bad conduct of our wives-for the subjects always tread the footsteps of their King.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.845,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-43-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7042017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1f092ce103936cbcf439e35c9e39d886aadf4480613d8a1580999e1ba0960429","compact":"fd313a63183fa219d840f457f4f2a33377f61870ca4416efb7aecbdcb4be1917","nasal":"cf4f1f3a4864b7084df4d1edfc48e9957db9a5dba9fd50828928f2c5e370feed"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-42-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":42,"verse":18,"english":"Rävaņa did forcibly place Sītā on her lap; how can then Rāma enjoy delight in her company? Having taken her to the city of Lankā, Rāvaņa did keep her in the Asoka forest and Sītā was brought under the control of Rākşasas. Still Rāma has not been worked up with hatred by Sītā. From now we shall also broke the bad conduct of our wives-for the subjects always tread the footsteps of their King.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.789,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-43-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7042018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. D